      "id": 1,
      "text": "West Glacier was renamed from Belton in 1949 to highlight its location, though the railroad station and chalet still carry the Belton name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Glacier%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Belton Chalet, built in 1910, survives today as a registered National Historic Landmark and one of Montana's grandest historic hotels.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Glacier%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "West Glacier sits at the western entrance to Glacier National Park, where the Middle Fork and North Fork of the Flathead River meet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
